       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 50 mg of amlodipine daily is five times the maximum dose. I don't know of any indication that justifies it. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I'd expect severe, prolonged hypotension and possibly shock, and the effect could last for days.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO daily**, the maximum labeled dose, if you want the strongest dosing.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** If the goal is more blood pressure control, I can add a second agent from another class instead.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy.** If you have a rationale I haven't considered, such as a protocol or a research setting, I can document it. That would still need to go through direct pharmacist review and your institution's override process, not through me.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
